---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="What is a QR Code and How Does It Work?"
  description="Learn what QR codes are, how they work, and how to create your own free QR code online."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">Published: October 2, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3">
        What is a QR Code and How Does It Work?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
        QR codes are everywhere — on menus, business cards, ads, and packaging. Here's
        what they are and how to make your own.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        QR stands for "Quick Response." A QR code is a square, black-and-white pattern
        that stores information — usually a URL, text, or contact details. When you scan
        it with your phone camera, that information is instantly read.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">How Does a QR Code Work?</h2>
      <p>
        A QR code stores data in a grid of tiny squares. The three large squares in the
        corners help scanners orient the code. The rest of the pattern encodes your data
        along with error-correction information, which lets the code still be readable
        even if part of it is damaged.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">What Can You Store in a QR Code?</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Website URLs</li>
        <li>Plain text messages</li>
        <li>Phone numbers</li>
        <li>Email addresses</li>
        <li>Wi-Fi network details</li>
        <li>Payment links</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">How to Create Your Own QR Code</h2>
      <p>
        Creating a QR code is free and takes seconds. Use our{' '}
        <a href="/tools/qr-generator" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
          free QR Code Generator
        </a>{' '}
        — enter your text or URL, choose a size, and download the PNG. No signup, no
        watermark.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Do QR Codes Expire?</h2>
      <p>
        Static QR codes (like the ones you generate here) never expire. They encode your
        data directly, so they'll work forever. Dynamic QR codes (used by some paid
        services) can expire if the subscription ends.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Final Thoughts</h2>
      <p>
        QR codes are a simple, powerful way to share information. Whether you're a
        business owner, teacher, or just someone who wants to share a link quickly, a
        QR code does the job. Try our{' '}
        <a href="/tools/qr-generator" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
          free QR Code Generator
        </a>{' '}
        to create yours in seconds.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <a href="/blog" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">
        ← Back to Blog
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>